/**
 * Solved heads-up preflop strategy at 100 big blinds.
 *
 * Generated by `scripts/generate-blueprint.ts` with
 * 20,000 iterations of vector CFR, converging to an
 * exploitability of 0.000001 big blinds per hand. Being two-player
 * and zero-sum, that number means what it says: no counter-strategy can beat
 * this one by more than that.
 *
 * Keys are `seat|hand|context|actions`, where seat 0 is the small blind —
 * heads-up, the button — and the action digits are fold(0), call(1),
 * raise(2), all-in(3). Values are the frequency of each, in the same order.
 *
 * Limping is not modelled; the opening decision is raise or fold. Everything
 * after preflop is priced by all-in equity adjusted for position rather than
 * played out. Do not edit by hand — rerun the script.
 */

